# Mac and Windows drop junk files into every folder they touch -- .DS_Store when
# a Finder window opens, Thumbs.db when Explorer renders a preview, ._ forks when
# a Mac copies onto a drive that is not its own. Nobody creates these on purpose
# and nobody wants them in a clone. This list is fixed rather than growing: the
# operating systems have written the same handful of files for twenty years.
.DS_Store
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Obsidian's per-device window layout (workspace.json on desktop,
# workspace-mobile.json on iPad and iPhone). The REST of .obsidian/ is tracked on
# purpose: app.json carries the vault's real settings, so any device that syncs
# this repo opens the vault already configured. These two are different. They
# record only which panes happen to be open on one device, they rewrite
# themselves constantly, and the iPad and a desktop each want their own. Tracking
# them buys a merge conflict on every sync in exchange for nothing.
.obsidian/workspace*.json
